success: true
exit_code: 0
----- stdout -----
Overlay environment manager for NixOS

Usage: nails [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  activate         Activate the hidden NixOS environment (mount overlayfs + switch profiles)
  deactivate       Deactivate and reboot into the decoy state (unmount + cleanup + reboot)
  emergency        Emergency mode: rapid deactivation with countdown
  status           Show current status and uptime
  verify           Verify system is clean of NAILS artifacts
  check            Check readiness to activate without making any changes (alias: doctor)
  init             Initialize NAILS directory structure on a hidden volume
  reset-upper      Delete a target's persistent overlay upper on the hidden volume
  config           Inspect and check the configuration file (nails.toml)
  notify-dispatch  Dispatch pending desktop notifications (called by XDG autostart on login)
  help             Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -c, --config <PATH>
          Path to the configuration file (overrides binary-relative discovery)

  -v, --verbose...
          More diagnostics on stderr: -v for debug, -vv for trace

  -q, --quiet
          Print only errors and the final result

      --color <WHEN>
          When to use colour

          Possible values:
          - auto:   Colour a stream only when it is a terminal, TERM is not `dumb` and NO_COLOR is unset or empty
          - always: Always colour, even when piped
          - never:  Never colour

          [default: auto]

      --ascii
          Use ASCII markers instead of Unicode symbols and box drawing

      --json
          Print machine-readable JSON on stdout

      --no-log-file
          Do not write the log file on the hidden volume (diagnostics still go to stderr)

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version

----- stderr -----
